---
import Layout from '~/layouts/LandingPage.astro';
import FAQs from '~/components/widgets/FAQs.astro';
import CallToAction from '~/components/widgets/CallToAction.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'FAQs',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- FAQs Widget ******************* -->

  <FAQs
    tagline="FAQs"
    title="Frequently Asked Questions"
    items={[
      {
        title: 'What kind of Apache Kafka deployments are supported?',
        description:
          "So far, we support self-managed deployments (either on-premises, or in the cloud) and AWS MSK. We do not support other managed Kafka providers such as Confluent, Aiven, Instaclustr, and others becuase they don't have the necessary configuration exposure to setup connectivity to Kinkang.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Why base Kinkang on Cruise Control?',
        description:
          'Cruise Control is an industry-standard tool for scaling and balancing Kafka clusters. It provides a comprehensive solution for managing Kafka clusters efficiently at an enormous scale.',
      },
      {
        title: 'How do we guarantee secure connectivity?',
        description:
          "For self-managed Kafka deployments, we support and recommend using security protocols such as SSL (for encryption) and SASL/PLAIN (for authentication) for secure communication over the public internet and we're flexible enough to adapt to any other security requirements. As for AWS MSK and GCP Kafka, we use can again choose between SSL + SASL/PLAIN over the public internet, or use AWS and GCP networking and security services like IAM authentication, AWS Private Link (or PNI) / GCP Private Service Connect, VPC peering, and others to securely connect to an AWS MSK or GCP Kafka instance.",
      },
      {
        title: 'What happens if Kinkang has an outage?',
        description:
          "Kinkang is designed to be resilient and fault-tolerant. But disasters do happen. In case of such, the main impact for our customers would be temporarily no workload rebalancing and no cluster scaling operations. But the Kafka cluster itself will continue to operate normally and as usual. We're NOT impacting the cluster's health and its critical operations in any way.",
      },
      {
        title: 'How do I have interact with my Kinkang instance?',
        description:
          'We offer an API that allows you to interact with your Kinkang instance. The API offers a manual rebalance mechanism, onboarding and offboarding of Kafka brokers (i.e. cluster shrink and cluster expansion), stoppage of an ongoing rebalance, cluster state querying, and more. This API can be used to create internal custom tools.',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </FAQs>

  <CallToAction
    id="contact-us"
    actions={[
      {
        variant: 'primary',
        text: 'Contact us',
        href: '/contact',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">Still have questions?</Fragment>
  </CallToAction>
</Layout>
